{
  "title": "Review R2a-2: report the delivered change's size against the request's stated budget (not blocking)",
  "body": "## Problem\nPart of M6.5, Epic R (#824), slice R2a-2.\n\nEvery actionable issue states a budget (docs/ISSUES.md: \"**Budget** … keep the budget small enough to review\"), and AGENTS.md asks each change to \"keep to its line budget … name any overrun in your report\". Nothing in the factory measures it. The orchestrator compares sizes by hand: #800 at 345 lines against 150, #810 at 329 against 150, #811 at about 300 against 100, and #842 at 2.3 times its budget.\n\n- **The audit's diff can't serve as the report's figure.**\n  - The audit stage diffs before delivery (`src/pipeline/engine.ts:1784`, `changeDiff` at :1503-1504; three-dot for verify-change).\n  - Delivery can then merge a newer base without another audit (`mergeForDelivery`, which updates `baseSha` at `engine.ts:3350`) before the report is rendered (`engine.ts:3120-3145`).\n  - Verify-change sets `run.baseSha` to the original PR head (`engine.ts:630`), while `changeDiff` diffs from `state.verification.baseSha` (`engine.ts:1501`).\n  - Delivery renders the report at seven places, `buildReportArtifacts` at `engine.ts:2748, 2987, 3003, 3011, 3076, 3093, 3144`. They include the already-merged recovery (~2983–2990) and the verification-only paths (~3000–3011), which return before ordinary delivery.\n  - The audit's `--numstat` call (`src/git/repos.ts:837`) leaves rename detection to the user's `diff.renames`, and mixes tests, docs and source in one total.\n- **The budget is in the run's request.**\n  - Issue-started runs carry the issue body as quoted JSON, recovered by `unquoteGitHub` (`src/integrations/github.ts:62`).\n  - Comment runs carry separate `request` and `issueBody` fields (`github.ts:93-101`).\n  - Hand-started runs carry the request text itself.\n- **The report has no size section** (`renderReport`, `src/pipeline/report.ts:103`). Its state input is an explicit `Pick` (`report.ts:74-91`).\n\n## Invariant\n- The report's Size section describes exactly the range the PR delivers, at the moment the report is rendered. It names that range's base and head SHAs and its mode.\n- It counts added plus removed lines, split into source, test and docs, against at most one budget figure, read only from the request as the run received it.\n- If the size can't be measured, or the budget can't be read as a single figure, the section says so.\n- No outcome depends on any of this.\n\n## Requirements\n1. **Parse the budget.** A pure `statedBudget(prompt)` in a new `src/pipeline/budget.ts`, returning `{ kind: \"figure\", lines, text } | { kind: \"zero\", text } | { kind: \"ambiguous\", text } | null`.\n   - **Sources, parsed independently:**\n     - issue runs: the issue body;\n     - comment runs: the comment's `request` first, then `issueBody`, using the first non-null result;\n     - other runs: the prompt.\n\n     Texts are never concatenated.\n   - **Removed first:**\n     - fenced blocks: an opening line of three or more backticks or tildes, closed by the same character at least as long;\n     - `\u003cdetails\u003e` … `\u003c/details\u003e` blocks, nesting counted. Issues keep their original description there, often with an older budget, for example #30's \"≤ 400 changed source lines\" next to its current \"roughly 80\".\n   - **The section:**\n     - a heading at any level whose text is exactly `Budget` (case-insensitive), up to the next heading of the same or a higher level;\n     - otherwise the first line starting, after any list marker, with `Budget:`, through the end of its paragraph.\n   - **Figures:** an integer (commas allowed, `1,200`) followed within three words by `line` or `lines`. A range `A–B`, `A-B` or `A to B` followed by lines counts as one figure, B.\n     - Exactly one figure, greater than zero: `figure`.\n     - Exactly one, equal to zero: `zero`, reported with no percentage.\n     - More than one: `ambiguous`.\n     - None: `null`.\n\n     `text` is the section clipped to 200 characters, after redaction.\n2. **Measure at every delivery render, through one helper.**\n   - A new async `renderDeliveryReport(ctx, success, verifiedFailure?)` calls `measureSize` and then `buildReportArtifacts`. Every delivery render uses it, replacing all seven direct calls. That includes:\n     - the already-merged recovery;\n     - the verification-only renders (verification failed; unchanged verified PR);\n     - the verdict-comment failure renders;\n     - the verified-draft render;\n     - ordinary delivery after any `mergeForDelivery`.\n   - `measureSize(cwd, base, head, mode)`:\n     - `base` is `ctx.state.verification?.baseSha ?? ctx.run.baseSha`, the same base `changeDiff` uses (`engine.ts:1501`);\n     - `head` is `HEAD` at render time;\n     - `mode` is `merge-base` for verify-change and `two-dot` otherwise.\n   - With no worktree or no base, it records `{ unavailable: \"\u003creason\u003e\" }` and runs no git command.\n   - Run it with `worktreeGit([\"git\", \"diff\", \"--numstat\", \"-z\", \"-M\", …])`.\n     - `-M` (git's default 50% similarity) is explicit, so the result doesn't depend on `diff.renames`.\n     - `-z` makes renames parse as `added removed \\0 old \\0 new \\0`, and lets paths containing tabs or newlines parse.\n   - **Categories:**\n     - **test:** a path segment `test`, `tests` or `__tests__`, or a basename matching `*.test.*`, `*.spec.*`, `*_test.*` or `test_*.*`;\n     - **docs:** matches the base commit's `[gates] docs` (`ctx.state.gatesConfig.docs`, via `globToRegex`);\n     - **source:** everything else.\n\n     Precedence is test, then docs, then source.\n   - **Renames** count their own edited lines (numstat for the pair), all in the destination path's category. A rename that crosses categories is also listed by both names. A pure rename counts zero.\n   - **Binary** entries (`-` `-`) count zero and are listed by count.\n3. **Record and report.**\n   - Save `ctx.state.sizeReport = { base, head, mode, source: {added, removed}, tests: {…}, docs: {…}, binary, renamesAcross: [...], stated }` before rendering. On a measurement error, save `{ base, head, mode, error }` with the error redacted.\n   - Add `sizeReport` to `ReportInput.state`'s `Pick`.\n   - `renderReport` adds `## Size`, for example: \"Source: +180/−40 (220 lines) against a stated budget of 150 (147%); tests +310/−12; docs +20. Range: `\u003cbase8\u003e..\u003chead8\u003e` (two-dot).\" For `zero`, `ambiguous`, `null` or an error, it says which, with the quoted budget text where there is one.\n   - Discreet repositories follow the report's existing publication path, with no factory marks added.\n4. **Not blocking.** No audit finding, gate verdict, review input, round decision or delivery step reads `sizeReport`, and a measurement error never fails delivery.\n\n## Tests\nEach must fail without its change. Unit tests for the parser; real git on a seeded fixture repository for the measurement and the delivery wiring.\n\n**Parsing**\n1. Each returns the stated result:\n   - `## Budget\\nAbout 80 changed source lines plus tests.` → 80;\n   - `Budget: about 120 source lines plus tests.` → 120;\n   - `## Budget\\nAbout 1,200 lines.` → 1200;\n   - `Budget: 100–150 lines` → 150;\n   - `Budget: 0 lines` → `zero`;\n   - `Budget: about 100 source lines; stop at 150 lines` → `ambiguous`;\n   - `Budget: 2 PRs` → `null`.\n2. **Removal (adversarial).**\n   - A `\u003cdetails\u003e` block, a backtick fence and a tilde fence carrying \"Budget: 999 lines\" are ignored in favour of the current `## Budget`.\n   - A `### Budget` nested under `## Plan` ends at the next `##`.\n3. **Sources.**\n   - A comment run whose `request` says `Budget: 50 lines`, with an issue body whose `## Budget` says 300, gives 50.\n   - With no budget in the request, it gives 300.\n   - An issue run reads its body, and a plain CLI prompt reads itself.\n\n**Measurement**\n4. A change of 100 source lines, 200 test lines and 20 docs lines reports exactly those numbers in `sizeReport` and in the rendered Size section.\n5. **Renames.**\n   - A 300-line file renamed with one line replaced counts 1 added and 1 removed (2 total), with `diff.renames=false` set in the fixture's git config.\n   - A source file moved into `test/` with one replaced line counts 2 test lines and is listed as crossing categories.\n   - A docs file moved into `src/` counts as source.\n   - A binary rename counts 0 and is listed.\n6. A path containing a tab or a newline is counted and classified.\n7. **The base's docs globs, not the change's.** A change that adds its own source directory to `[gates] docs` in `.limitless.toml` still counts that directory as source.\n\n**Delivery**\n\n8. **Base advance.** The base gains a commit between audit and delivery, and the delivery merge brings it in. `sizeReport.base` is the new base, the counts exclude the base's commit, and the section names the new range.\n9. **Resume after that merge:** a restart after `mergeForDelivery` and before the report re-measures the same range and renders one Size section.\n10. **Error.** A measurement failure, injected through the fake git runner, renders \"Size unavailable: …\", and delivery completes with the same PR state as without this change. A missing worktree or base renders the explicit unavailable result.\n11. **Not blocking.** A change at 500% of its budget yields the new `sizeReport` numbers and Size section, with audit findings, gate verdicts and the round count identical to a run without this change.\n12. **Verify-change base.** An unchanged verified PR, delivered through the verification-only path, reports its non-empty diff against `verification.baseSha`, not the zero diff against `run.baseSha` (its own head).\n13. **Already-merged recovery.** A run resumed after its PR merged renders the Size section through the helper on the early-return path.\n14. **One helper.** Every delivery render site reaches `measureSize`: a test drives each of the seven paths and finds a Size section, or an unavailable result, in each saved report.\n\n## Compatibility\n- **Rollback:** `sizeReport` is an optional `RunState` field, and the previous release ignores it. PR bodies gain one section; readers of PR bodies (land and the review verdict) don't read it.\n- **Restart and resume:** the size is recomputed deterministically from the stored range at every delivery render. No new side effects.\n- **Polling only:** no involvement.\n- **Hot path:** one `git diff --numstat` per delivery render.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Blocking on, or escalating, overruns.\n- Feeding the size into review, Epic D or P3's calibration (they read `sizeReport` later).\n- Counting by language, and detecting generated files beyond the test and docs classes.\n- The audit stage's own diff and summary (unchanged).\n- The mutation check (R2a-1) and docs against the current base (R2a-3).\n\n## Budget\nAbout 135 changed source lines plus tests: the parser ~45, measurement and classification ~35, the shared helper and its seven call sites, state and error handling ~35, the report section and `Pick` ~20. Stop at 175 and report.\n"
}
